WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:05.240
We always seem to end up back
to basically us, with something

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.800
a little bit different,
Spock for example.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.280
-Did he always have a bowl cut?

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.240
Think he always had a bit of a bowl.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.960
Leonard Nimoy's bowl.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.120
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.080
Predator is a guy in a suit,
Spock, a guy with false ears.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.920
Then of course we've got
the archetypal alien.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.120
-In every case it's basically
a humanoid body shape.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.640
-All of these seem to lack
a bit of imagination to me,

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.720
looking at them from an
evolutionary perspective.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.840
There's going to be some rules.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.280
I think it's going to be
carbon based,

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.760
microbes are going to be important.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.800
We're going to see
natural selection and evolution.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.520
If I could make one bet about
alien life, it would be on that

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.120
it would evolve and I don’t think
I would lose this bet.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.560
A very great thickness of ice, about
10 miles I think, and underneath

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:22.000
we've seemingly got good evidence
that there is liquid water.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.240
I think it's all heated by
these volcanic vents.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.240
Which is looking a little bit similar

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.880
to the sorts of things that we find

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.440
in the deep ocean here on Earth.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.640
We know there's going to be
no sunlight getting down.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.880
So they're going to have
to be chemosynthetic.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:48.560
Bacteria would maybe, at some point,
start to form symbiosis, larger cells

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:53.320
and then you would have maybe
the beginnings of multicellular life.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:59.400
Because this is an unstable planet,
any kind of life around these vents

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.320
needs to have a mobile form.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.720
It has to be able to abandon ship
and find new vents to live on.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.560
-I mean let's imagine we find
something like this tadpole creature.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:12.920
It doesn't have eyes
because it's dark.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:13.960
-Yeah it's dark down there.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.520
-But he does have some way
of sensing heat.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.800
Let's imagine this guy is actually

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.520
the first morph
of a more complex organism.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:24.800
Maybe you would see
him metamorphosing.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:32.360
He is now turning into his real form,
a kind of chemosynthetic large worm.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.040
He takes root actually.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.720
-So he's attaching just like
the larvae of a sea squirt

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.320
that we find here on Earth.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:41.200
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.120
-These mobile forms that can
find new habitat and then start

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.480
the whole thing all over again.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.120
He's using his tentacles as gardens
to cultivate these bacteria and to

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.480
charge his metabolism.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:56.120
When this probe lands in 15 years,
we might be proven right,

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.760
something like this
might be down there.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:07.240
When Trappist is orbiting its sun,
it stays tidally locked, which means

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:11.040
the same face is always facing the
sun. One side is getting absolutely

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.360
baked whilst the other side gets
no light at all and is very cold.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:18.240
And that line where sun meets shade,
this terminator as it's called,

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:21.520
is the zone where life might just
about be able to exist on Trappist,

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.880
like a long thin island of life.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.480
-One side is always sunny,
and one side is always dark.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.440
So that would imply constant winds,
flowing one direction.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:35.720
What pass off as trees
could be like weather veins.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.920
You can see this effect
on Earth actually,

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.560
if you go to the edges of cliffs.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.760
You know with that strong wind
blowing, it's going to be quite

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.680
difficult for these animals
to make themselves heard.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.000
I think we're going to see
animals displaying.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.560
-Maybe among the trees you see
something red fluttering about,

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:59.280
like a kite.
This quasi-bird-like animal,

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.120
with a very long snout and
he uses it to hold onto the tree.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:10.160
And what he then does is,
open up his cape like wings...

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.360
He's trying to attract a mate?

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.720
Yeah he's trying to impress
his potential girlfriend here.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.480
-Very colourful world.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:18.320
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.400
But a very focused and intense world.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:25.000
So imagine a line of predators
that always stalk from the

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.200
direction of the sun.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.680
Maybe he would have six limbs,
rather than four.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.960
-Which gives you a huge advantage
for hanging on and for

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:34.960
clambering around.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.920
There's no reason at all why this
animal couldn't have an extra joint,

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.560
giving it a little bit more range of
movement, more flexibility because

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.880
with that lower gravity
it's not taking such a strain.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:48.200
Raptorial legs,
legs that can grab and hold.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.400
It gives it a huge reach!

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:51.360
Watch your back...

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.240
Yes!

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.240
Very high gravity
is going to be a big issue.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:03.960
-Everything is kind of
flattened out, maybe one form

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:07.720
could be like this
flattened slug creature.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.960
-Flat worm sort of creature?

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:14.200
You could have a huge variety
of these guys.

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:17.760
Given that the planet has been around
for two billion years longer

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:21.440
than Earth has, might we find the
evolution of intelligent life?

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.960
Because of the size constraints,
I think intelligent life would begin

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:29.640
from a colonial perspective,
just like a group of ants

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:30.840
collaborating together.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:36.000
If you were to see these guys,
they would look like very

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:41.480
intelligently guided swarm of little
shapes, moving across the floor

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:43.040
and coming towards you.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:46.520
Maybe they would form
different shapes or letters,

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:47.840
trying to communicate.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:51.320
-The idea of all these subunits,
these little individual things coming

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:55.160
together and creating not just a
colony but something that’s got

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:58.320
intelligence and can travel across
space, really appeals to me.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:07.840
Certainly the whole issue of
contamination by alien bacteria.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:12.040
I think it's the one thing
we can't protect against.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:15.120
It's what we saw in the history,
the recent history, of humans.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:18.120
As we've gone across through the
world spreading things like smallpox,

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:21.240
so in a way that's a study
in miniature of what would happen

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.240
perhaps if an alien culture
were to come here.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.840
We're going to need some
sort of galactic quarantine.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:28.040
Yeah, or a galactic hospital!

